0 !ACHILLES {"id":"ACH-Z02-S01","name":"Zone II · Scene 1: City at Peace — Torchlit Bridal Procession","zone":"Z02","lines":"18.491–496","greek":"Ἐν δὲ δύω ποίησε πόλεις μερόπων ἀνθρώπων καλάς. ἐν τῇ μέν ῥα γάμοι τ᾽ ἔσαν εἰλαπίναι τε, νύμφας δ᾽ ἐκ θαλάμων δαΐδων ὕπο λαμπομενάων ἠγίνεον ἀνὰ ἄστυ, πολὺς δ᾽ ὑμέναιος ὀρώρει· κοῦροι δ᾽ ὀρχηστῆρες ἐδίνεον, ἐν δ᾽ ἄρα τοῖσιν αὐλοὶ φόρμιγγές τε βοὴν ἔχον· αἱ δὲ γυναῖκες ἱστάμεναι θαύμαζον ἐπὶ προθύροισιν ἑκάστη.","buckley":"On it also he fashioned two beautiful cities of articulate-speaking men. In the one, indeed, were marriages and feasts; and they were conducting the brides from their chambers through the city with brilliant torches, and many a bridal song was raised. The young men were dancing in a circle, and among them flutes and lyres gave forth their sounds; and the women standing, each at her portals, admired.","worldModel":{"vision":"White marble colonnades and golden-linteled portals illuminated by trans-orange torches (3959), festive white/gold/lilac chitons, and golden lyres.","memory":"Processional state transition: brides advance from domestic chambers (θάλαμοι) through public avenues as youths whirl in circular dance.","controller":"Civic kinship and celebration: acoustic synchronization of hymenaeus song, aulos flute, and phorminx lyre."}}

